invariant: INV-11
file: quic.c
catches: quic_loop_test
reason: ch_quic_seal hands quic_packet_seal a Key Phase bit of 0 in place
  of q->key_phase, so after a key update every 1-RTT packet names the
  first phase while it is sealed under the new keys, and the peer opens
  none of them. test/quic_loop_version.h updates the server's keys and
  requires the client to open the next packet with its next set.

--- old
                                q->key_phase, pn, pn_len, hdr, hdr_len, pt, pt_len, out, cap,
--- new
                                0, pn, pn_len, hdr, hdr_len, pt, pt_len, out, cap,
